# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React + Vite project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version managed by npm)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with dependency resolution

### 2. Code Changes
**Modified: client/src/App.jsx**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `BrowserRouter` in the main App component
- Placement ensures Speed Insights tracking works across all routes

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite projects:
- Used the React-specific package export: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Added the component at the root level of the application for comprehensive tracking
- No additional configuration required - the component works automatically when deployed to Vercel

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ No breaking changes to existing functionality
✅ All dependencies properly resolved
✅ Production build generated without issues

## Next Steps

When deployed to Vercel:
1. The Speed Insights script will automatically load
2. Performance metrics will be collected from real user visits
3. Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights

No further action required - Speed Insights will begin collecting data once deployed to Vercel.
